From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ruskin Constant <ruskin@cloudflare.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 11:18:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Enable clip-rule, flood-color and lighting-color in the servo
 build

Same pattern as the earlier gecko-gate removals (accent-color, break-*,
background-clip:text). These three SVG and filter-effects longhands
have no servo-specific representation issue: clip-rule's FillRule and
the Color type of flood-color and lighting-color are already compiled
unconditionally for servo (used by clip-path, path(), fill, stop-color
and others). Dropping engine = "gecko" lets servo parse and compute
them. Nothing downstream consumes them for paint, since SVG filter
primitives aren't implemented, which matches other parse-only
properties.
---
 properties/longhands.toml | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/properties/longhands.toml b/properties/longhands.toml
index 0f82a7b..3e5758a 100644
--- a/properties/longhands.toml
+++ b/properties/longhands.toml
@@ -544,7 +544,6 @@ servo_restyle_damage = "rebuild_stacking_context"
 type = "FillRule"
 initial = "Default::default()"
 struct = "inherited_svg"
-engine = "gecko"
 animation_type = "discrete"
 spec = "https://svgwg.org/svg2-draft/masking.html#ClipRuleProperty"
 affects = "paint"
@@ -835,7 +834,6 @@ affects = "layout"
 type = "Color"
 initial = "computed::Color::BLACK"
 struct = "svg"
-engine = "gecko"
 spec = "https://drafts.fxtf.org/filter-effects-1/#FloodColorProperty"
 affects = "paint"

@@ -1238,6 +1236,5 @@ affects = "layout"
 type = "Color"
 initial = "computed::Color::WHITE"
 struct = "svg"
-engine = "gecko"
 spec = "https://drafts.fxtf.org/filter-effects-1#LightingColorProperty"
 affects = "paint"
